# Record bundles are addressed by SHA-256 from the reviews that cite them, so
# their bytes must survive a round trip through git unchanged. With
# core.autocrlf=true -- the default on the Windows machine these were produced
# on -- git stores LF and checks out CRLF, so the working copy hashes to one
# value here and another on Linux, and the digest printed in a review is then
# only verifiable on the machine that wrote it. That is the exact portability
# defect the bundles exist to remove.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line translation: what is committed is what is
# checked out, on every platform.
C1_RECORDS_*.json -text
